 p=P.read_text();p=re.sub(r'object%20accounting-[0-9.]+%25','object%20accounting-90.67%25',p,count=1);p=re.sub(r'\*\*Verified translated instruction bytes:\*\* \*\*[0-9,]+\*\*','**Verified translated instruction bytes:** **213,069**',p,count=1);p=re.sub(r'\*\*Reconciled object bytes:\*\* \*\*[0-9,]+ / 239,698 = [0-9.]+% \([0-9.]+%\)\*\*','**Reconciled object bytes:** **217,336 / 239,698 = 90.6708% (90.67%)**',p,count=1);p=re.sub(r'\*\*Unresolved object bytes:\*\* \*\*[0-9,]+\*\*','**Unresolved object bytes:** **22,362**',p,count=1);P.write_text(norm(p.rstrip()+'''\n## Batch 90 — view/grid initialization\n\nAdded **280 translated instruction bytes**, bringing accounting to **213,069 translated + 4,267 non-code = 217,336 / 239,698 = 90.6708% (90.67%)**. `334C4` derives the grid-cell count from `25619*2561B`, clears bit 6 in each low flag byte, selects the two view-table entries through `C65C/C658`, derives signed/low-word sweep step state through the two `35680` calls, initializes the four sign-extended edge globals, then transfers control to the already translated `32954` sweep. Next frontier: **`335DC`**.\n'''))
 a=A.read_text();A.write_text(norm(a.rstrip()+'''\n## CODE.2 Batch 90 checkpoint\n\nBatch 90 reconciles `334C4..335DB`: **280 translated bytes** and no separator bytes. Coverage is **217,336 / 239,698 = 90.6708% (90.67%)**, with **22,362 unresolved bytes**. Preserve the binary's do/while grid clear (including its zero-count wrap behavior), `C65C` dynamic table addressing, argument order for both `35680` calls, full result stores before low-word truncation/negation, and signed-word expansions from `255EE/255F6/255D6/255D2`. Next frontier is `335DC`.\n'''))
